	(text "RAILS (record section 10): independent bucks from +BUS, the record's \"likely\" topology.\nTPS54560B x3: 60 V in, 5 A, SO-8 PowerPAD (gull-wing, hand-solderable), one design laid out three times.\nInput headroom: bus clamps at ~45 V, part is rated 60 V.\n+12V: regen clamp supply (must self-start, no enable from firmware), fan, accessory 12 V.\n+5V: stamp VIN (pin 14; stamp makes its own 3.3 V for the P4), drive 485_5V (comms pin 10), AHCT125.\n+3V3: INA228, RS485 transceiver, pull-ups, accessory 3.3 V.\nTODO(detailing): FB dividers, COMP network, RT/CLK frequency (keep all three identical,\nconsider sync to stagger), input MLCC at each VIN pin, EN/UVLO. D2-D4 60 V 5 A Schottky.\nLAYOUT: amp-class switch nodes vs the INA228 resolving +-5 uV is the most likely respin cause (section 10).\nKeep SW nodes small and far from R2 / INA228. Accessory power connector: open item on SPEC.md."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 130 120 0)
		(effects
